3. **The change.** In `b595-fix`: save `sha256` of `package.json` and `package-lock.json`; run the method; assert `package.json` unchanged; run Proofs 1, 2, 4, 5 and the Behaviour smoke. Re-run `npm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund` once: the lock must be byte-identical (a fixed point, as rehearsed; if not, say how it differs).
4. **Commit, once.** `git add package-lock.json` only. Message: first line `deps: body-parser 2.3.0 -> 2.4.0 (lockfile only; GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828, high) <ticket key>`; a body in the shape of `6a69fdf4` / `c139e4a8`: the advisory and its range, which lock keys changed and why each (express `^2.2.1` admits 2.4.0; the other three are body-parser 2.4.0's own higher floors), "package.json is byte-identical to main", the predicate with its exit status before (main, exit 1) and after (head, exit 0), the verify counts before and after, "the lock is a fixed point of npm install --package-lock-only"; trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; no person's name. Do not claim what you did not run (for example "sending mail" or any DoS behaviour).
5. **Property checks, push.** See THE PROPERTY CHECKS. Push exactly one branch.

## THE PROPERTY CHECKS, then commit and push
(a) `git diff --name-only <main sha>..HEAD` is exactly `package-lock.json` (control: a planted second path is flagged); `package.json` sha256 equals main's (`e4e38291...`, quote the full value you read). (b) `git diff <main sha>..HEAD -- . ':!package-lock.json'` is 0 bytes (control: a range holding a source change is nonzero). (c) 0 non-ASCII bytes added (`git diff <main sha>..HEAD | LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c -E '^\+.*[^ -~]'` = 0; control: a planted byte counts 1). (d) no `node_modules`, `session-tools`, `audit.json` or scratch tracked or staged. (e) gitleaks over the range and the message (`/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks` if present; a random `ghp_`-shaped canary fires rc 1, then the real scan rc 0, chained with `&&` in `bash -c`; the repo's own rule: `gitleaks dir .` is NOT a local gate, RD-111, scan the commit range; the lock holds `sha512-` integrity strings, so say whether the lock-file rule (RD-115) fired). (f) `git rev-list --left-right --count <main sha>...HEAD` = `0 1`; `merge-base --is-ancestor <main sha> HEAD`. (g) the path intersection printed again. Push exactly one branch, plainly (never force): `GIT_SSH_COMMAND="ssh -i '/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/3_Access_Keys/github_deploy_rw' -o IdentitiesOnly=yes"` under `/bin/bash`, `git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/b595/nexusai-body-parser-audit`; a publickey denial is transport (retry 5 times about 10 s apart, C-192); GH013, "protected branch", "rejected", non-fast-forward are STOPs. Read the ref back with `ls-remote` AFTER the last push.

